\title{
Quantum $K$ theory for flag manifolds
\author{Givental, Shrair}
\abstract
The classical GKM formula has been extended to incorporate operations on $K$ theory for the complete flag manifold within a semisimple algebraic group. This extension enables the demonstration that certain operators preserve a specific class of functions under the application of a particular combinatorial structure known as the Berenstein-Gelfand graph. Consequently, it follows that the complete flag manifold's GKM presentation yields explicit descriptions of both the classical and quantum $B$-affine Grassmannian's $K$-representing functions, as well as their relationship to affine Grassmannian $K$-homology. Moreover, a new set of relations has been established for the quantum $B$-affine Grassmannian's $K$-representing functions, incorporating deformation parameters into the quantum Berezin relations for the positive half of the affine Grassmannian.
